@startuml current_cache_classes
title Current cache responsibilities - main bd42eea01 (before this PR)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
left to right direction

class "_ensure_csrc_cache.yaml" as Ensure <<workflow>> {
  source_ref / optional fixed rebase
  target_ids
  +resolve_targets()
  +lookup_four_arm64_ubuntu_L0_targets()
  +build_missing_targets()
}
class "_build_csrc_cache.yaml" as Producer <<workflow>> {
  resolved target / csrc_hash
  +restore_L1()
  +compile_on_CPU()
  +verify_native_extension_exists()
  +save_L1_and_L0()
}
class "resolve_csrc_cache_targets.py" as Resolver <<script>> {
  +resolve_targets(target_ids)
}
class "csrc_cache_targets.json" as Targets <<configuration>> {
  image / runner / architecture / SOC / OS
}
class "csrc-l1-restore / csrc-l1-save" as Transport <<composite actions>>
class "csrc/build.sh + build_cache.py" as Engine <<build engine>> {
  +validate_inner_content_keys()
  +restore_or_compile_units()
  +prune_after_success(max_versions=2)
}
class "_selected_tests.yaml\nand regular source-build consumers" as Tests <<workflows>> {
  +restore_L0()
  +compile_with_L1_on_miss()
}
class "_schedule_image_build.yaml" as Image <<workflow>> {
  +restore_L0()
  +build_Dockerfile(compile_on_miss)
}
class "_nightly_image_build.yaml" as NightlyImage <<workflow>> {
  +extend_runtime_image()
  +publish_nightly_image()
}
class "three _e2e_nightly_single_node* workflows" as Single <<workflows>> {
  +restore_L1_for_PR_source()
  +install_PR_source()
}
class "_e2e_nightly_multi_node.yaml\n+ multi_node/run.sh" as Multi <<workflow + Pod script>> {
  +use_PVC_local_build_cache()
}
class "GitHub Actions Cache" as GHA <<artifact store>>
class "OBS: ascend-ci-cache-hk" as OBS <<snapshot store>>
class "Container registry" as Registry <<image store>>

Ensure --> Resolver
Resolver --> Targets
Ensure --> Producer : missing targets
Ensure ..> OBS : baseline L0 lookup configuration
Producer --> Transport
Producer --> Engine
Transport --> OBS : L1 snapshots
Producer --> OBS : baseline L0 save configuration
Tests --> OBS : baseline L0 restore configuration
Tests --> Transport : L0 miss
Image --> GHA : L0 restore without explicit S3 configuration
Image --> Registry : runtime image
NightlyImage --> Registry : consume runtime / publish nightly
Single --> Registry : use nightly runtime
Single --> Transport : direct L1 restore (baseline)
Multi --> Registry : use nightly runtime

note bottom of Ensure
  Four explicit coordinator lookups are not a generic
  image matrix. Configured image tags can differ from
  the actual Dockerfile FROM tags.
end note
note bottom of OBS
  Baseline mixes explicit S3 configuration and implicit backend selection.
  Links describe workflow-level configuration, not runner-injected settings.
  Target design makes L0 explicitly GitHub Cache.
  L1 retains its existing OBS transport.
end note
legend bottom
  Classes model code responsibilities; workflow files are not Python classes.
  This diagram describes the pinned baseline, not the partially edited candidate.
endlegend
@enduml
